===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|walden|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|wealdan||to rule, control, determine, direct, command, govern, possess, wield, exercise, cause, bring about|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|waldanan|to rix, reign|lang=en}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|waldʰ-|to be strong, be powerful, prevail, possess|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|walten||to prevail, reign, dominate|lang=de}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|volde||to cause|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|valda||to cause|lang=is}}, {{etyl|lt|-}} {{term|valda||land property|lang=lt}}, {{etyl|lt|-}} {{term|valdyti||to rule|lang=lt}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|UK|_|dialectal|ambitransitive}} To [[govern]]; [[inherit]].

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|wald|lang=enm}}, {{term|iwald|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|geweald|ġeweald|might, power, possession, control, command, dominion, bridle, protection, subjection, groin, pudenda|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|gem-pro|waldan|might, power, main|lang=en}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|waldʰ-|to be strong, be powerful, prevail, possess|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Gewalt||force, power, control, violence|lang=de}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|våld||force, violence|lang=sv}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|UK|_|dialectal}} [[power|Power]]; [[strength]].
# {{context|UK|_|dialectal}} [[command|Command]]; [[control]]; [[possession]].

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|wield}}


